# The in-mesh WARNING debt the samples trees carry, for `mw-plugin-test compile
# --warning-baseline`. Format: `<NodeType path> <diagnostic id>`, `#` comments, blanks ignored.
#
# 🚨 SHRINK-ONLY, and the gate holds you to it in BOTH directions:
#   * a (type, code) pair that is NOT listed FAILS the bake — the debt cannot grow back;
#   * a listed pair whose type compiled CLEAN of that code is STALE and FAILS the bake until the
#     line is deleted — so paying a debt down is not optional bookkeeping.
# A listed type that did NOT compile this run is UNVERIFIABLE, never stale: it produced no
# warnings at all, and reading that silence as "the debt is paid" would delete a real record on a
# measurement nobody took.
#
# 🚨 TWO RATCHETS, one file, split by the code — see Doc/Architecture/InMeshWarningStandard.
#   * CS1591 is documentation debt and has its own verdict, so a missing doc comment can never be
#     the reason an unrelated change cannot merge.
#   * everything else is a latent bug or a doc comment that is actively WRONG.
#
# 🚨 THIS IS NOT A PLACE TO PUT A DIAGNOSTIC YOU DID NOT WANT TO FIX. Three whole codes that this
# file would otherwise have carried were fixed at the ROOT instead, because the platform — not the
# content — emitted them, and baselining them would have recorded the generator's debt under the
# content's name in every repo of the fleet:
#   * CS0105 (119 occurrences / 23 types) — the skeleton generator concatenated every source
#     file's `using` lines without de-duplicating them, so correct authored source earned "the
#     using directive … appeared previously". Fixed in DynamicMeshNodeAttributeGenerator.
#   * CS1591 × 2 per type (54 sites) — the generated `…MeshNodeProviderAttribute` and its `Nodes`
#     property are public and were undocumented. No author could ever have fixed those. Fixed by
#     generating the doc comments.
#   * CS8632 (21 types) — authored `string?` in a tree with no `#nullable` directive. Fixed with
#     NullableContextOptions.Annotations (the annotation context only — no nullable analysis).
# Measured before/after on this tree: 850 raw occurrences over 27 of 27 types → 375 over 18.

# ── CS1591 · missing XML doc comment (the doc-comments ratchet) ────────────────────────────────
# 362 occurrences over 271 distinct members in 17 NodeTypes, all of it authored sample content.
# Every line here is one NodeType's worth of undocumented public API; delete the line the day that
# type is fully documented — the gate will tell you, by failing on the stale entry.
ACME/Article                CS1591
ACME/Project                CS1591
ACME/Project/Todo           CS1591
FutuRe/BusinessUnit         CS1591
FutuRe/ExchangeRate         CS1591
FutuRe/GroupAnalysis        CS1591
FutuRe/LineOfBusiness       CS1591
FutuRe/LocalAnalysis        CS1591
MathDemo/Matrix             CS1591
Northwind/AnalyticsCatalog  CS1591
Northwind/Article           CS1591
Northwind/Customer          CS1591
Northwind/Employee          CS1591
Northwind/Product           CS1591
Northwind/Supplier          CS1591
PensionFund/Position        CS1591
PythonDemo/PrimeReport      CS1591

# ── CS1701 · assembly-reference version skew (the warnings ratchet) ────────────────────────────
# 🚨 The ONE class of entry here whose owner is the REFERENCE SET rather than the content:
#   "Assuming assembly reference 'System.Linq.Expressions, Version=8.0.0.0' used by
#    'System.Reactive' matches identity '…, Version=10.0.0.0' … you may need to supply runtime policy"
# System.Reactive is compiled against .NET 8's System.Linq.Expressions and runs on the .NET 10
# shared framework. No content author can fix it and no `#pragma` belongs in their source; the
# honest outcome is that the bake RECORDS it. It lands on exactly the types whose compile binds Rx,
# so a line goes stale when a type stops using it — which is the ratchet working, not churn.
ACME/Article                CS1701
ACME/Project                CS1701
ACME/Project/Todo           CS1701
FutuRe/GroupAnalysis        CS1701
FutuRe/LocalAnalysis        CS1701
Northwind/AnalyticsCatalog  CS1701
Northwind/Article           CS1701
Northwind/Customer          CS1701
Northwind/Employee          CS1701
Northwind/Product           CS1701
Northwind/ReportsCatalog    CS1701
Northwind/Supplier          CS1701
PythonDemo/PrimeReport      CS1701
